    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Hogans Corner sits at the crossroads of State Routes 109 and 115, anchoring the community in western Grays Harbor County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hogans_Corner%2C_Washington",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The area was once part of the traditional lands of the Quinault and Quileute tribes, who lived in permanent villages along rivers and the Pacific shoreline.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hogans_corner_washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the mid‑1800s, settlers cleared land for potatoes and grazing, often traveling by canoe or overland trails from Oregon, though many abandoned claims due to isolation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hogans_corner_washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The local water system draws from two wells to supply potable water to Hogans Corner, Illahee, and Oyehut, solving historic utility challenges.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hogans_corner_washington",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Coastal tides shape 4.3% of the CDP, creating a dynamic wetland environment influenced by the Grays Harbor estuary.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hogans_corner_washington",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Hogans Corner experiences a temperate marine climate with average annual rainfall of about 68 inches, mostly from October to April.",
